st/hooks/codex/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n120:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/completion-evidence-stop.cjs\", type: file_exists }\n121:   - { host: codex, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/scripts/session-cleanup.sh\", type: file_exists }\n122:   - { host: codex, event: PreCompact, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/compact-inject.js\", type: file_exists }\n123:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-start.js\", type: file_exists }\n124:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js\", type: file_exists }\n125:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n126:   - { host: devin, event: PreToolUse, path: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n127:   - { host: devin, event: SessionStart, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n128:   - { host: devin, event: UserPromptSubmit, path: \".skilled/hooks/goal/devin/goal-inject.mjs\", type: file_exists }\n129:   - { host: devin, event: Stop, path: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/session-stop.js\", type: file_exists }\n130: \n131: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n132: # INPUTS\n133: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n134: inputs:\n135:   none: \"This diagnostic takes no arguments. Every checker derives its expected state from the canonical trees and the runtimes' own config files.\"\n136: \n137: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n138: # EXECUTION\n139: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n140: execution:\n141:   steps:\n142:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees, all four hook discovery mirrors and the .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ links into the hook library. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n143:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n144:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n145:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error (bad argument, canonical dir missing, or crash).\"\n146:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_body_parity with --all. Compares each agent body across the runtime trees; same-file mirrors and non-comparable formats are reported, not counted as matches. Exit 0 = all comparable mirrors in sync, 1 = drift or comparison failure, 2 = checker invocation error (unknown option), 3 = not checkable (frontmatter parser unavailable).\"\n147:     - \"Run upstream_assets.command_catalog. Compare command frontmatter with the root and family indexes and hub metadata. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = checker error.\"\n148:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check --allow-worktree. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .skilled adapter no longer exists on disk. Explicit OK output = in sync; a drift report = drift; refusal, error, or missing affirmative output = error.\"\n149:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n150:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n151:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_skills, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/skills/ links. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n152:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_prompts, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/prompts/*.md files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n153:     - \"Run upstream_assets.dsh_agents, the command node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check. Covers the generated .dsh/agents/*.patch.yml files. When .dsh/ is absent, report the row as n/a (no .dsh/ tree) without running the check; an n/a row leaves STATUS unchanged, and this run never creates that directory. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n154:     - \"For each row in hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks, run its file_exists check (a plain path-existence read, no execution of the adapter or the shell command that wraps it). Collect every row whose path does not resolve as a degraded hook adapter, keyed by host:event:path.\"\n155:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n156: \n157: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n158: # OUTPUT\n159: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n160: output: |\n161:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH row while its runtime tree is absent.\n162:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n163:     runtime mirrors  -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n164:     codex agents     -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n165:     codex prompts    -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n166:     codex hooks      -> node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n167:     agent body parity (.skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs) -> .claude/agents is a hand-maintained real-file mirror; update both its .skilled source and Claude twin, then run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs for .codex/agents, node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs for .pi/agents, and node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs for the .cursor and .devin links\n168:     pi agents        -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n169:     pi prompts       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n170:     dsh skills       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-skills-dsh.cjs\n171:     dsh prompts      -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-prompts-dsh.cjs\n172:     dsh agents       -> node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dsh/sync-agents-dsh.cjs\n173:     command catalog  -> update the root and family indexes, group counts, and hub metadata from command frontmatter\n174:   While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), never in sync, and leave\n175:   STATUS unchanged: the mirror does not exist yet, and this run never creates it. Their repair lines are the generators without --check, run once the tree exists.\n176:   The agent roster check has no generator. Its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n177:   for the authored surfaces (.skilled/agents and .claude/agents).\n178:   Hook CONFIG STRUCTURE is deliberately out of scope for mirroring: the four runtimes use incompatible event\n179:   vocabularies and entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked\n180:   against each other.\n181:   Separately, \"N hook adapters degraded to fallback\" reports the count of hook_adapter_fallback_health_checks\n182:   rows whose path does not resolve, each listed as host:event:path. This is the same drift a live adapter\n183:   failure produces (its fallback JSON would carry \"mkHookDrift\": true and its stderr a matching\n184:   \"mk-hook-drift host=<host> event=<event> adapter=<name>\" line) surfaced without needing to fire the hook or\n185:   read raw JSON. Repair is adapter-specific: rebuild the runtime (npm --prefix\n186:   .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build) for a dist/hooks/* path, or restore/recreate the named\n187:   script for a .skilled/bin or .skilled/hooks path.\n188:   STATUS=ERROR when a checker refuses to run, returns an error, or omits an affirmative result."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528095755,"end":1794528096118}}}}
